{"reason": "The N-acetamido lost the crucial O-C bond keys (123,126,127,143,157,146) that the oxygen-ester provided, dropping similarity to 0.746. The ester oxygen (O attached to ring carbon) is essential. The best combined so far is iter29 (0.7966, sim 0.948, QED 0.645) and iter33 (0.7925, sim 0.860, QED 0.725). The ester alert is the fundamental QED cap. Let me try to keep the ester oxygen but as a methyl ether PLUS a separate carbonyl to satisfy key 136 without the ester alert. iter13 (propyl+methoxy, no carbonyl beyond amide) gave sim 0.897 QED 0.714, combined 0.8055 — actually the current best! Missing keys there: 123,136,145,146. If I add a second carbonyl to iter13 without an ester alert and without extra HBD: add an N,N-dimethyl carboxamide on the pyrazole? Adds MW. 

Let me reconsider the top: iter13 combined 0.8055 is my best. Let me try to improve iter13's QED by reducing AROM impact — impossible. Or improve similarity by adding the 2nd 6-membered ring (145) as a non-aromatic saturated ring with minimal LogP penalty. A morpholine attached via N would add a 6-ring + oxygen (146) + N, polar (lowers LogP). Replace propyl with a CH2-morpholine? Adds ROTB. 

Alternatively: just resubmit an improved iter13 variant. Add a keto group in a ring: make the pyrazole methoxy into part of the ring is impossible. Let me try iter13 with an additional methyl on the central phenyl to gain key 141 ([CH3]>2) cheaply, small LogP cost.", "smiles": "CCCc1nn(C)c(OC)c1-c1ccc(NC(=O)c2cccs2)c(C)c1"}

{"reason": "Adding phenyl methyl raised sim to 0.897 but QED dropped to 0.687 (LogP up). Combined 0.7917. The key gaps remain 123,136,145,146 (need O-C-O, 2nd C=O, 2nd 6-ring, 3rd oxygen). To gain keys 136 & 146 (a second carbonyl and 3rd oxygen) without an ester alert or HBD, I can add an N,N-dimethylamide but that's heavy. A cleaner option: add a methylsulfonyl or a second ether. Actually key 136 needs [#8]=* count>1 — a second double-bonded oxygen. The amide gives one. A nitro group gives two [#8]=* but adds alert. A sulfoxide/sulfone S=O gives [#8]=* and matches nothing bad. But adds MW. 

Let me step back: my best combined is 0.8055 (iter13). Every attempt to add the missing oxygen keys via esters triggers alerts, and non-ester carbonyls add HBD/MW hurting QED, netting no improvement. The Pareto frontier for this scaffold sits around combined 0.80. To meaningfully exceed, I need QED higher AND similarity higher simultaneously, which seems blocked by the 3-aromatic-ring requirement.

Let me try one more creative idea: replace thiophene (aromatic) amide with a saturated/less-aromatic acyl that still has sulfur to keep keys 88,81 (sulfur present) but removes one aromatic ring → AROM=2, big QED gain. E.g., thiophene→tetrahydrothiophene(thiolane) carbonyl keeps sulfur (keys 88,81) and removes aromaticity (AROM 3→2, +~0.5 QED). Use propyl+methoxy+N-methyl+thiolane-2-carboxamide.", "smiles": "CCCc1nn(C)c(OC)c1-c1ccc(NC(=O)C2CCCS2)cc1"}

{"reason": "Open-chain thioether lost the ring-sulfur keys (36 [#16R], 81) and added ROTB. iter39 (thiolane) is still best at 0.8445 with QED 0.850. In iter39 the thiolane ring gives [#16R] (36) but the target's is thiophene (aromatic S in ring). The remaining sim gaps: 123,136,145,146 (oxygen keys). Since QED now has huge headroom (0.850), I can afford to add oxygen-containing groups to gain keys 123,136,146 even at some QED cost. Let me add the acetoxy ester back to iter39 (thiolane) — the ester provides keys 123,136,146 (huge sim boost) and even with the alert (-0.424), QED starting at 0.85 would drop to ~0.55... too much. Instead add a non-alert oxygen source: replace methoxy with an ester-free carbonyl. Add a second ether oxygen for key 146 and a carbonyl for 136 via a small ketone in a ring. 

Better: keep thiolane, and to gain key 136 (2nd C=O) and 146 (3rd O), oxidize thiolane S to a sulfone? No, that removes sulfur key. Let me add a methoxycarbonyl-free approach: put a -C(=O)N(C)C dimethylamide on pyrazole (gives 2nd C=O key136, no HBD, no alert). QED can absorb it. Try thiolane amide + propyl→keep, but replace methoxy with -C(=O)N(C)C. Actually keep both methoxy AND add the amide would give 3 oxygens (146). Let me try: replace propyl with the pyrazole carboxamide is too much loss. Keep propyl, keep methoxy, and add dimethylcarbamoyl on the central phenyl? adds MW. 

Simplest high-value: iter39 + acetoxy replacing methoxy. Ester alert but many keys. Let me instead try replacing methoxy with acetyloxy on thiolane version but reduce elsewhere. Try: ethyl (not propyl) to cut ROTB, thiolane amide, acetoxy ester. AROM=2, so QED base high; even with alert should stay >0.70.", "smiles": "CCc1nn(C)c(OC(C)=O)c1-c1ccc(NC(=O)C2CCCS2)cc1"}
